**How to implement.** Copying experiments brings the kit profiles their data is mapped by, because a profile lives in the kit file, not in the experiment (001 §H 'Between kits'; .spec-md §3.15; step 291: a copy keeps each experiment's profile name and row selection; S6's rule that a clashing name takes the next free suffix). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, at its end: `type ImportProfileName with member this.nextFreeAmong (taken : ImportProfileName list) : ImportProfileName`, the `ImportProfileName` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` (step 255) over the taken names' `FileStem.ofText`, the one suffix sequence items, setups and experiments use. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`: `ExperimentCopyReport` (steps 224, 227) gains, as its last fields, `profiles : ImportProfile list` (each profile the copy added to the kit file, as added) and `kitFile : KitFile` (the kit file as the copy left it). `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` (steps 224, 227, 261, 290, 291) keeps its read-then-write order and its errors: after the kept experiments it takes, in order of first appearance, the distinct profile names of their `dataOpt` that `ChosenImportProfile.tryOfName source.kitFile.importProfiles` (step 300) answers as `KitProfileChoice` (a built-in or an unheld name needs nothing). A profile the target holds under that name with equal content is reused; one the target holds under that name with other content is added as the source's profile named `nextFreeAmong` of the target's names and the ones added before it, and the copied experiments mapped by it name the new name; any other is added as it is. When it adds any, it writes `this.saveKitFile { this.kitFile with importProfiles = this.kitFile.importProfiles @ <the added> }` (step 131) after the data files and before any setup or experiment, so a written experiment never names a profile the kit lacks; its `KitError` is `KitLibraryKitErr`. `kitFile` is that saved kit file, else `this.kitFile`. No merge or replace of a held profile is added. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `CopyChosenExperiments` (steps 225, 227, 261) sets the window's content over `{ model.kit with kitFile = report.kitFile }`, so the window holds the profiles the copy added; its texts are unchanged. Tests. `KitTests` gains `a profile name takes the first free suffix among the taken ones`: `(ImportProfileName "Lab scan").nextFreeAmong []` is itself, over `[ Lab scan ]` is `Lab scan (2)`, and over `[ Lab scan; LAB SCAN (2) ]` is `Lab scan (3)`. `ExperimentCopyTests` (step 224) gains `a copy brings the kit profiles its experiments use, reusing an equal one and renaming a different one`: the source's kit file also holds a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column) and E1 is mapped by it, E3 by `Intensity series`; copying [E1; E3] into a target whose kit file holds another `Lab scan` (its σ column 5) leaves the target's kit file, read back through `readKitFile`, holding its own `Lab scan` and the source's as `Lab scan (2)`, the copied E1 mapped by `Lab scan (2)` and E3 by `Intensity series`, and the report's `profiles` exactly the one added; copying E1 into a target holding an equal `Lab scan` adds no profile, writes the kit file not at all, and keeps E1's profile name. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 225): `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source` also has the source's kit file hold `Lab scan`, saved through `saveKitFile` before the source is closed, with E2 mapped by it, and asserts that `model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles` and the target's `readKitFile` hold `Lab scan` after the copy. Every other copy fact passes unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After a copy carries profiles, `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` MUST add each kit profile its copied experiments are mapped by, reusing an equal one and renaming a different one by `ImportProfileName.nextFreeAmong`, before it writes any experiment, and the window MUST take the kit file it left; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a profile name takes the first free suffix among the taken ones` and `a copy brings the kit profiles its experiments use, reusing an equal one and renaming a different one`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
